Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Four-, Five- and Six-Point QED: Construction and Checks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"5ca1b447-bdbb-4884-877e-3bc950bf458e"],

Cell["Evaluate Setup once, then evaluate any individual calculation below. The 36 explicit calls cover all photon-helicity assignments at fixed external ordering: 5 four-point, 10 five-point and 21 six-point tree amplitudes of the electron/photon QED model. Each result has a distinct qed4..., qed5... or qed6... variable, so later calculations do not overwrite it. The wrapper displays progress, total time and all final checks before returning a validated expression. Some completion paths remain unresolved and are labeled beside their calculation cells. All momenta are ingoing. Other external label orderings follow by particle relabeling; pure-photon trees and charge-unbalanced processes vanish. Massive fermion spin dependence remains symbolic.", "Text", ExpressionUUID->"456f9b3b-17be-418a-8209-5779a70c7365"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4816341a-7984-4b8b-988a-1a38dedfcf65"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
hepcatDirectory = ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
$HEPCATpath = FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"source\"}];
Get[FileNameJoin[{$HEPCATpath, \"HEPCAT.wl\"}]];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[104]:=",ExpressionUUID->"502400f7-a148-4769-998b-3289c5a54045"],

