Cell["Use the cubic QED model for every diagram calculation and for four-point factorization. The model containing known four- and five-point amplitudes supplies five- and six-point factorization. Neither model is changed.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e40be2b8-a07c-4c47-93ff-40449897d0a0"],

Cell["diagramModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"models\"}], 2];\nfactorizationModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \"models\"}], 3];\nelectronMass = ModelParameter[diagramModel, \"Me\"];\nelectricCharge = ModelParameter[diagramModel, \"EE\"];\n", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[107]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f61894d2-c74b-4610-a3de-e1941760c4ae"],

Cell["\<\
The independent benchmark uses the massive-QED Feynman model. Its own model \
file specifies the same numerical electron mass and charge as the \
constructive QED example. Each model retains its own parameters; no global \
parameter assignments or symbol substitutions are needed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e949351-7167-4e81-83a5-e5d0eebf69c2"],

Cell["\<\
qedFeynmanModel = ReadModel[FileNameJoin[{hepcatDirectory, \
\"model_feynman\"}], 2];\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[101]:=",ExpressionUUID->"39ecf8f2-3357-45c7-b69b-99fa03763f4d"],

Cell["\<\
The amplitudes retain symbolic Me and EE. Numerical checks and completion use \
the parameter values and derived functions from the supplied model. PASS \
means agreement at the tested samples, not a general analytic proof.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43f1ccea-2be0-4dac-abdd-f6a191035779"],

Cell["The construction wrapper chooses its calculation settings automatically, reports progress and elapsed time, and returns the expression only when all required checks pass. The one option shown below supplies the independent Feynman benchmark model; it does not tune the calculation. Other options are needed only to override a default.", "Text", ExpressionUUID->"ec7e2a65-5ad5-54a8-b037-0c605814a7c6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Four-Point Amplitudes", "Subtitle", ExpressionUUID->"058277b2-d0a3-505b-bd1a-c27c47ce0997"],

Cell["Five separate calculations: every two-photon helicity assignment and four-fermion scattering. Four-point factorization uses the same cubic model as the diagrams.", "Text", ExpressionUUID->"b73eb392-82ee-5711-a971-c472ac8ca249"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,A.+,A.+", "Chapter", ExpressionUUID->"44abe297-98a2-5c63-9e22-20132a3d21cb"],

Cell["qed4PP = ConstructAmplitude[\n  {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\"},\n  diagramModel, diagramModel,\n  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]", "Input", ExpressionUUID->"90196480-cbbe-591b-86bf-9971ced0f0e4"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,A.+,A.-", "Chapter", ExpressionUUID->"6c528ba2-0997-5b0a-8471-8891d0a6212b"],

Cell["qed4PM = ConstructAmplitude[\n  {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.-\"},\n  diagramModel, diagramModel,\n  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]", "Input", ExpressionUUID->"ea0cf00e-74e4-5d70-b283-9e93b492ddf2"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,A.-,A.+", "Chapter", ExpressionUUID->"c06e2ad2-6d65-59ba-bbe3-82f1c184d0dc"],

Cell["qed4MP = ConstructAmplitude[\n  {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.-\", \"A.+\"},\n  diagramModel, diagramModel,\n  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]", "Input", ExpressionUUID->"2d47318b-2768-54aa-a153-5b151237d8e0"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,A.-,A.-", "Chapter", ExpressionUUID->"1dd37843-dab3-5b64-8f91-00d69cbd1ee0"],

Cell["qed4MM = ConstructAmplitude[\n  {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.-\", \"A.-\"},\n  diagramModel, diagramModel,\n  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]", "Input", ExpressionUUID->"ff9a4ce7-51eb-5dd2-83c5-4752ef20edcf"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,E,e", "Chapter", ExpressionUUID->"ca8c8a3a-7428-5eea-9858-ee4650553a52"],

Cell["qed4FourFermions = ConstructAmplitude[\n  {\"e\", \"E\", \"E\", \"e\"},\n  diagramModel, diagramModel,\n  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]", "Input", ExpressionUUID->"30016c22-1f87-58da-9f86-9762ba2239bd"]

}, Open]]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Five-Point Amplitudes", "Subtitle", ExpressionUUID->"14d58ea4-5912-556a-a5f4-303fde3d68aa"],

Cell["Ten separate calculations: all eight three-photon helicity assignments and both helicities for four-fermion photon emission.", "Text", ExpressionUUID->"6e4d3289-7533-59da-b218-9fccf89d4647"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["e,E,A.+,A.+,A.+", "Chapter",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001759665590519*^9, 
  4.00175967079949*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4254fc93-7cf4-42a6-a5cc-\
47271d455e72"],

Cell["Construct and Check", "Section", ExpressionUUID->"4bb6cc79-e5b1-5881-9b17-76788c5ed6fd"],

Cell["Evaluate this cell after Setup. The wrapper generates and prepares the diagrams and factorization channels, completes and prepares the amplitude, then runs all final checks. The printed test report precedes the returned expression. The saved manual work remains available below.", "Text", ExpressionUUID->"39cf6e8f-7d10-5f73-a8f3-e11920c14eca"],

Cell["qed5PPP = ConstructAmplitude[\n  {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\"},\n  diagramModel, factorizationModel,\n  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel]", "Input", ExpressionUUID->"fc84dd4f-fa99-5122-82eb-b35b4a28e6ce"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Earlier Step-by-Step Work (Optional)", "Section", ExpressionUUID->"7369c4b7-f770-5019-b403-b20fd89d7ae9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Choose the Process and References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a25b4f6c-ab7e-4178-82c7-1af73d66324e"],

Cell["\<\
Start with the all-plus example. To explore another process, change particles \
and reevaluate Sections 1-5. Completion supplements sewn channels with verified \
reference alternatives without changing the prepared diagrams. It refits failed \
validation samples within explicit limits. A bounded correction space can still \
be insufficient; UNRESOLVED is not a completed amplitude. Existing worked \
derivations are shown separately below.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"884df899-0624-455e-ac77-ff3789ad9b73"],

Cell["\<\
particles = {\"e\", \"E\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\", \"A.+\"};
referenceChoice = \"AllSpurious\";\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016723486207333`*^9, 4.001672391849534*^9}, {
   4.001757782755148*^9, 4.00175778752351*^9}, 4.001757993489561*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[113]:=",ExpressionUUID->"59e9054c-37eb-4d9b-9009-ab266ff680e0"],

Cell["\<\
Other examples are {\"e\",\"E\",\"A.+\",\"A.+\",\"A.-\"} and {\"e\",\"E\",\"E\
\",\"e\",\"A.+\"}. Reference choices: Automatic; \"AllSpurious\" (cyclic \
other massless particles); \"AllPhysical\" (momentum-insertion references \
outside the diagram's own poles); \"Xi\" (one common Xi0); \"IndependentXi\"; \
\"ReverseCyclic\"; None (unchanged). The referenceChoice variable controls \
the preparation in Section 3.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"381d17af-a09d-4116-8fd8-3524916bcd57"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Generate the Diagrams", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"db43e89f-6886-4c59-b8e6-bfcf66576fc6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
diagrams = CreateDiagrams[particles, diagramModel];
rawAmplitudes = diagramAmplitudes[diagrams];
Length[rawAmplitudes]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[115]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2cf0490d-3446-4e8f-8f1f-5f2d05171f2d"],

Cell[BoxData["6"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0016721377967997`*^9, 4.0016879511169777`*^9, 
  4.0020168126609573`*^9, 4.002021500272408*^9, 4.002028527826282*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[117]=",ExpressionUUID->"a832d5fe-a895-4f71-9bfa-e6e79f3a8bdb"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The all-plus process has six diagrams. rawAmplitudes keeps each expression \
together with that diagram's mass rules.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99bed7d4-df64-4bc9-a7e3-460737ceb805"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["View the diagrams", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f30e05cf-6e77-4326-97b4-d9c6741dc99e"],

Cell["CreateArrowDiagrams[diagrams]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e6e7e4e9-1352-4ac9-8f16-31a663ee659e"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Prepare Each Diagram", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d7eb1abf-cdef-4adf-b490-a6d9f152e8a2"],

Cell["\<\
Preparation applies ReduceSpinContractions, selects the references, reduces \
known numerator scalar products, calls ReduceSpinorProducts, then continues \
with improving identity steps. Each diagram uses its own internal on-shell \
conditions in its numerator. Original propagators stay off shell.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a7164525-9dfc-4fd1-ae72-3cb18a63da1c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
preparationDetails = PrepareAmplitudes[rawAmplitudes, diagramModel,
  \"ExternalParticles\" -> particles,
  \"PolePreference\" -> referenceChoice,
  \"ReturnDetails\" -> True];
preparation = preparationDetails[\"PreparedAmplitudes\"];
preparation\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[118]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ec1714ca-a64e-4304-b156-d264fbcc9cb0"],

