Cell["\<\
These small sample counts are for an interactive example. The fit and \
validation use different kinematic samples with the model's parameter \
values. Increase them, and add other theory-consistent \
ValidationParameterRules, for a more extensive test. Success at this stage \
establishes only the sampled physical-factorization constraints.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dad05d55-8a15-4c63-b152-f6e9c8db42ea"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Complete High Energy and Verify", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"809fa82c-a8c5-49e4-9431-d37a2d9a84a9"],

Cell["\<\
Run this stage only after factorization is complete. It checks physical residues again, together with high-energy growth, spurious-pole cancellation and explicit Xi independence. It does not necessarily find the shortest expression.

Completion returns {externalMassRules, expression}. The check below first uses PrepareAmplitudes to simplify that completed pair. Only external on-shell rules are retained; no internal numerator on-shell conditions are applied.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8f05d2eb-7bef-45ae-b9b3-774c335de9a4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["completion = If[FailureQ[factorization] || factorization === $Failed,\n  factorization,\n  CompleteHighEnergy[factorization, channelPreparationDetails, factorizationModel]];\ncompletion", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9c8b8417-1b8b-4a2e-acce-77e8a1662191"],

