data. Two modular diagnostics gave coefficient rank 2576 and augmented rank \
2577. This is evidence of a missing direction in that finite ansatz, not an \
exact rational impossibility proof. No exact fit or successful \
CompleteFactorization result is claimed for that space; the explicit \
lower-amplitude recursion above is a different, justified construction.",
          "Text"]}, Closed]]}, Open]],
   Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["4. Independent Checks", "Section"],
      Cell["The Feynman diagrams are generated only now, after the \
constructive amplitude. Their internal lines remain off shell. Keep all \
checker rows visible: PASS means agreement at the tested samples; an \
unsupported factor or timeout is UNRESOLVED, not success.", "Text"],
      Cell["feynmanDiagrams = CreateDiagrams[particles, qedFeynmanModel];\nfeynmanPairs = diagramAmplitudes[feynmanDiagrams];\npreparedFeynman = PrepareAmplitudes[feynmanPairs, qedFeynmanModel,\n  \"PolePreference\" -> \"AllSpurious\"];", "Input"], Cell["constructionChecks = CheckAmplitudes[\n  constructedAmplitude, channels, factorizationModel,\n  \"FeynmanAmplitudes\" -> preparedFeynman,\n  \"FeynmanModel\" -> qedFeynmanModel, \"Output\" -> \"Details\"];\nconstructionChecks[\"Table\"]",
       "Input"], Cell[CellGroupData[
        {Cell["Inspect the Constructed Expression", "Subsection"],
         Cell["constructedAmplitude", "Input"]}, Closed]]}, Open]]
}, Closed]]
}, Open]],

